.TH MDT.RECOVERY_TOP 4 2026-08-23 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
recovery_top \- slowest clients per phase in the current recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdt." TARGET ".recovery_top"
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param obdfilter." TARGET ".recovery_top"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param mdt." TARGET ".recovery_top=clear"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDT or OST target device
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B recovery_top
parameter reports, for each of the three recovery phases, the
.B N
filesystem clients that took the longest to complete that phase, sorted
descending by delay, as three YAML lists named
.BR client_reconnect_top ", " client_req_replay_top " and"
.BR client_lock_replay_top .
Each entry reports a client
.RB ( nid )
and its delay
.RB ( delay_sec )
in seconds. Delays are measured from the start of recovery, so a client's later
phases include the time spent in the earlier ones. The depth
.B N
is set by the module parameter
.BR recovery_top_n " (default 10, max 64)."
The depth applies per phase, so up to 3 * N entries can be printed.
The lists are reset when recovery begins, and writing any value clears all
three phases.
.PP
This is the bounded-cardinality companion to
.BR recovery_histogram (4):
the histogram tells you the per-target distribution, this file tells
you which specific clients drove the tail.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B mdt.*.recovery_top
.B obdfilter.*.recovery_top
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the slowest clients on an MDT after a recovery:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl get_param -n mdt.lfs-MDT0000.recovery_top"
client_reconnect_top:
- { nid:   "192.168.101.7@tcp101", delay_sec:  47 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.4@tcp102", delay_sec:   8 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.3@tcp102", delay_sec:   7 }
client_req_replay_top:
- { nid:   "192.168.101.7@tcp101", delay_sec:  61 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.4@tcp102", delay_sec:  33 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.3@tcp102", delay_sec:  32 }
client_lock_replay_top:
- { nid:   "192.168.101.7@tcp101", delay_sec:  64 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.4@tcp102", delay_sec:  41 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.3@tcp102", delay_sec:  40 }
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B recovery_top
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" commit v2_17_53
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.recovery_delay (4),
